WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Good to have you on Tesla Short's time, episode 545.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.000
Patrick here in Vancouver, it's July 18th, 2026.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.220
Here's what's happening with Tesla today.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:12.720
Fran's Von Holtzhausen, receiving

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.320
the first protected Model S signature unit,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.200
shows Tesla still values its design heritage,

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.680
even as focused shifts to new platforms.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.960
The Q2 earnings preview returns attention to Optimus

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.260
and CyberCab after both programs

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.280
missed first half volume targets.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.440
Remember, the show covered Optimus on July 17th

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.980
with Gigatex's factory construction underway,

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:39.880
and volume production still targeted for 2027+.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:44.240
Tesla will report Q2 results on July 22nd.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:47.160
The call is expected to include updated timelines

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:50.040
that affect 2026 cash flow assumptions.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:54.700
Semi-production continues with a $27.6 billion

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.800
valuation reference attached to the program.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:02.280
Guidance is also anticipated on internal Optimus deployment

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.360
before any external sales begin.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.360
This connects directly to the open question

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.140
of when hundreds of units per week might appear.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:13.860
Now shifting to how the supervised autonomy stack

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.600
is evolving in the near term.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.460
Elon Musk confirmed that upcoming FSD versions

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:22.300
will log driver interventions and preferred routes.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:26.160
Remember, the show covered FSD unsupervised

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.700
on July 17th with supervised miles

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:31.460
still expanding ahead of regulatory review.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.520
The system will move from uniform behavior

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.460
across all vehicles to individualized patterns.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.520
Examples include express lane preference

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:41.840
or habitual exits.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:45.980
This change builds on the supervised stack already deployed

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:47.740
and aims to increase adoption.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.180
Regulators will still require the base safety case

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.160
before any unsupervised release.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.920
Early intervention data will feed the next training cycles

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.260
at cortex clusters.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.400
The feature addresses one of the open questions

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.800
around FSD unsupervised by moving beyond

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.560
one size fits all behavior.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.000
From software personalization,

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:11.140
the focus turns to physical movement

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.820
of the next generation fleet.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.860
Multiple cybercab units were photographed

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:18.400
secured on a Tesla semi-transporter.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:22.560
Remember, the show covered cybercab on July 17th

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.040
after the Wii robot unveiling with regulatory approval

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.840
still the primary gating item.

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.620
The sighting confirms ongoing movement

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:33.320
of the robot taxi vehicles between facilities.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:36.340
It follows the Wii robot unveiling

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:39.540
and precedes any public unsupervised operations.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.660
Viewers can track whether similar convoys

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.780
appear on public roads in coming weeks.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:47.760
The transporter itself is part of Tesla's

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.360
expanding semi-production that last appeared

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:53.380
in fleet testing coverage on July 17th.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.140
This movement supports the broader timeline

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.680
for initial fleet deployment

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.700
once regulatory approvals clear.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:02.860
The production start date and initial fleet size

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.620
remain the key open questions.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:08.200
On the regulatory front, the NTSB report

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.740
states the driver over-road autopilot

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:12.860
immediately before the fatal incident.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.640
Investigators examined vehicle logs

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:17.820
showing the sequence of control inputs.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:20.520
The finding adds to the ongoing record

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.800
of supervised system edge cases.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:25.920
Tesla has not yet issued a public response

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:27.460
to this specific report.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.120
The report focuses on the final seconds

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.900
of driver input rather than system performance.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:36.760
Future regulatory reviews of supervised autopilot

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:38.900
will likely reference this sequence data.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:42.200
This adds to the record of supervised system

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.720
edge cases under review.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:45.480
From safety scrutiny,

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.600
the conversation moves to longer term

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.400
product durability questions.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:52.780
European data shows Hyundai and Kia vehicles

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:56.040
retaining higher battery capacity after several years

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.900
than comparable Tesla models.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.700
The metric reflects real world degradation

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:03.460
under mixed climate and charging conditions.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:07.260
Tesla's larger installed base provides more data points

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.800
but also more variability.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:12.760
Future 4680 pack chemistry will be watched

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.600
for any reversal of this ranking.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.680
The gap appears across multiple model years

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:18.900
and usage patterns.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:22.720
Residual value calculations for used Tesla vehicles

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.400
in Europe may incorporate these health figures

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.540
in coming quarters.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:30.100
Battery health rankings in Europe expose a gap

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:33.100
between advertised range and retained capacity

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.500
after years of use.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:38.600
European data places Hyundai and Kia ahead of Tesla

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:39.460
on this metric,

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:41.780
despite Tesla's larger sample size

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.160
and different duty cycles.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:46.540
The difference matters because fleet operators

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:49.640
and used car buyers increasingly price vehicles

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:53.340
on measured degradation rather than initial EPA numbers.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.760
Real world charging habits and climate exposure

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:58.840
vary widely across the continent,

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:02.200
yet the ranking holds across multiple model years.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.340
This pattern suggests that initial range claims alone

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:08.200
no longer determine long-term ownership costs.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.080
Tesla's approach has long emphasized software updates

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.900
and thermal management to slow capacity loss.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:18.120
Yet the published European figures show rivals

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:21.740
achieving slower fade with conventional liquid cooled packs.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:25.240
One explanation lies in cell chemistry selection

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:28.220
and charge protocols that prioritize longevity

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:30.020
over peak energy density.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:34.880
If the gap persists into the next generation of 4680 cells,

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:36.800
it will affect residual values

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:39.080
and therefore the total cost of ownership,

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:41.740
Tesla can advertise to commercial customers.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:44.620
Lenders already adjust residuals

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:48.180
when degradation data diverges from manufacturer claims.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:51.420
Sustained underperformance on health would raise

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:53.560
the cost of capital for Tesla buyers

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:55.880
and compress margins on vehicles sold

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.980
into high utilization fleets.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.620
Closing that gap requires more than range improvements.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:04.420
It requires chemistry and software choices

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.560
that demonstrably protect capacity

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:08.760
over the vehicle's full service life.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:11.000
Future pack revisions will need

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:14.000
to demonstrate measurable gains in retained capacity,

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:16.660
not only in laboratory cycle tests,

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:18.900
but in the mixed use conditions captured

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:20.400
by the European data set.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:22.200
From measured degradation,

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:25.420
the discussion shifts to near-term market share signals

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:25.980
in Europe.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:29.140
Tesla captured the largest share of applications

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:31.640
under Germany's refreshed incentive program

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:32.840
in the opening weeks.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:35.600
The result reflects strong model Y

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:38.820
and Model 3 availability relative to competitors

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.920
still ramping compliant inventory.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:44.900
Subsidies apply to both private and commercial purchases.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:48.560
The next data point will be July registration figures

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:50.180
showing whether the lead holds.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:53.720
Early uptake data positions Tesla ahead of rivals

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:56.200
still adjusting to the new incentive structure.

00:06:56.820 --> 00:07:00.000
This lead could influence second half European volume

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.100
if the pattern continues into August.

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.220
From current sales momentum,

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:07.180
the story turns to internal design continuity.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.960
The designer of the Model S received

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:15.240
VIN001 of 250 of the limited signature edition.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.980
The car received paint protection film,

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.620
ceramic coating and additional protective measures.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:22.900
This allocation recognizes

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:26.000
Von Holtzhausen's long role in shaping Tesla's

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.000
exterior language.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:30.260
The choice signals that core design continuity

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:33.040
remains visible even as production emphasis

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:34.500
moves to newer lines.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.880
Next to watch is whether similar protected units

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:40.400
appear for other long-tenured team members.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:44.820
The signature series itself is capped at 250 units,

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:47.840
underscoring the exclusive nature of the allocation.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:51.300
Tesla posted that direct rides in FSD

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.880
supervised vehicles convert skeptics

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.980
more effectively than marketing materials.

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:59.580
The statement aligns with the company's ongoing push

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:03.480
to expand supervised miles ahead of any regulatory review

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:05.440
of unsupervised operation.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:09.100
Data from these rides feeds the next training cycles.

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.540
The next milestone remains the same

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:13.600
measurable reduction in interventions

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:15.400
on complex city streets.

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:19.240
This approach continues the supervised expansion path

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:22.060
last reviewed on July 17th.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.980
Real-world ride data also supports the shift

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:26.760
toward personalized preferences

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:28.400
now entering development.

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:31.740
The article surveys current humanoid deployments

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:34.500
across manufacturers and notes that most remain

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:37.100
in pilot or low volume internal use.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:40.520
Tesla's Optimus program is listed among those

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:43.860
still scaling from prototype cells at gigatexus.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:48.340
Volume targets for 2027 remain the key open question

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.060
for external sales economics.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:53.080
Observers will watch for the first sustained

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:54.420
weekly production cadence.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:57.660
The gigatexus dedicated factory construction

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:00.760
continues on the timeline last covered July 17.

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:03.580
Initial internal deployment targets

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:05.740
inside Tesla facilities will provide

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:07.780
the first measurable production data

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:09.860
before any external sales begin.

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:14.140
Tesla will repurchase Model 3 and Model Y units

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:16.080
that were built for the Canadian market

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:17.860
but entered the United States.

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:21.040
The action addresses import compliance requirements.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:24.020
Affected owners will receive buyback offers

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:26.240
rather than retroactive certification.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:29.800
The program is limited to the identified vins

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:32.500
and does not affect domestically produced vehicles.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:36.680
The recall targets only the specific cross-border imports

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.500
and leaves US built inventory untouched.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:43.100
Owners of affected vehicles will receive direct outreach

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.060
from Tesla with buyback terms.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:49.120
Agility robotics opened a new humanoid training facility

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:50.960
near Tesla's Fremont plant.

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:53.720
The location places a direct competitor

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:56.800
