00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:13.880
in the same markets Optimus targets.

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:18.000
Proximity to Fremont may also influence talent movement

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.380
between the two programs.

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:22.920
Tesla is adding dedicated semi-charging sites

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:24.840
as production volume increases.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:27.580
The expansion supports fleet customers

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:29.020
testing longer routes.

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:32.620
Megacharger compatibility and site power levels

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:33.960
are the immediate focus.

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:37.040
The next indicator will be how many additional

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:39.980
customer fleets sign on once the network reaches

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:41.360
stated coverage targets.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:44.460
This build out follows the first public

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:48.220
megacharger opening covered on July 17th.

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:50.280
Expanded coverage will directly test

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:52.320
the long haul economics that remain

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:54.820
the central open question for the semi-program.

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.540
Miami joins the list of cities

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:59.540
with planned Robotaxi coverage

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:02.520
while Texas operations increase vehicle counts.

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:05.140
The moves test permitting pathways

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:08.200
ahead of any unsupervised regulatory approval.

00:11:08.740 --> 00:11:10.460
Fleet growth numbers will be compared

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:12.440
against earlier internal targets.

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:16.180
The expansion builds on the initial Texas deployments

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:17.260
already underway.

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:20.720
Miami permitting will serve as an early indicator

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:23.000
of how other major markets approach

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.460
Robotaxi operations.

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:27.800
The Chinese SUV undercuts the model Y

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:30.280
by roughly that margin in its home market.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:34.200
Early European pricing rumors suggest similar positioning

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:35.640
once exports begin.

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:39.460
Tesla's response will likely center on software features

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:42.700
and supercharger access rather than matching the sticker.

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:46.100
The price gap appears across multiple trims

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:47.160
and battery options.

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:50.460
European buyers will see whether the difference holds

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:52.160
after tariffs and incentives.

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:56.140
Hyundai, Kia, and Rivian models keep physical buttons

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:57.780
and traditional gauge clusters

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:00.180
while pricing below the model Y.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:03.780
The design choice preserves familiarity for buyers

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:05.560
who prefer tactile controls.

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:09.320
Tesla's screen-only approach remains a differentiator

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:11.980
that some competitors have chosen not to copy.

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:14.800
The button retention appears consistent

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:17.860
across the three rivals despite different price points.

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:20.700
Buyers weighing the trade-offs will compare

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:22.820
long-term software update access

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:24.900
against immediate physical controls.

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:27.400
There is a challenge worth discussing.

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:30.400
The piece argues that Musk's public profile

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:33.100
and divided attention across multiple companies

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:36.140
now represent Tesla's primary external risk.

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:39.020
It contrasts this with earlier periods

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:41.960
when product competition alone defined the narrative.

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:45.600
Tesla's ability to maintain execution discipline

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:48.660
while the CEO's time is split will be tested

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:50.320
in the second half of the year.

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:53.740
The argument centers on how investor perception

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:56.760
of divided focus could affect valuation multiples

00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:59.600
even if operational metrics remain steady.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:03.120
Execution on the July 22 earnings call

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:05.240
